      "content": "The idea of trying to keep up when the tide is already rising is just a cruel joke. That constant pressure, the city breathing down your neck, is a constant reminder of how much you're fighting against. If all you truly crave is quiet, maybe the most immediate relief is to find a way to make that silence happen, even if it's just for a moment. Don't try to swim anymore; just find the quietest place to rest.",
